                        "glosses": [
                            "To lower physically."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8916008-3dc7-45f7-a0e0-292a24df9fb1",
                                "sense_id": "abb5258b-f6f4-32a5-8d0f-f35d768110b2",
                                "text": "[God had] Embast the valleys, and embost the hills."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5118b43-6f5c-3893-8e15-3aa750664359",
                        "entry_id": "edd788b1-eabd-348a-a73e-8a3a4224ed45",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To bring down or lower in position, status, etc.; to degrade, humiliate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d38e4f9-c04d-46d8-afa1-4b72b3b9d96b",
                                "sense_id": "d5118b43-6f5c-3893-8e15-3aa750664359",
                                "text": "And either vowd with all their power and witt\n To let not others honour be defaste\n Of friend or foe, who ever it embaste […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38f04872-1fdc-4fe9-b94b-e65cba614e9b",
                                "sense_id": "d5118b43-6f5c-3893-8e15-3aa750664359",
                                "text": "Such pitiful embellishments of speech as serve for nothing but to embase divinity."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "546c373a-7237-394f-8f94-5691a873c88b",
                        "entry_id": "edd788b1-eabd-348a-a73e-8a3a4224ed45",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To lower the value of (a coin, commodity etc.); to debase (a coin) with alloy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6c1929c-1459-4d60-9962-4908ec0c82f8",
                                "sense_id": "546c373a-7237-394f-8f94-5691a873c88b",
                                "text": "Alloy in coin of gold […] may make the metal work the better, but it embaseth it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
